---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import content from '../../i18n/en/docs';
import { t } from '../../i18n/ui';

const lang = 'en';
---

<Layout
  title="Documentation — CIPHER-MUX"
  description={content.hero.body}
  lang={lang}
  active="docs"
>
  <div class="docs-page">

    <!-- Anchor Nav -->
    <nav class="cm-anchor-nav">
      <div class="cm-anchor-nav-label">{t(lang, 'scroll.label')}</div>
      {content.sections.map((section) => (
        <a href={`#${section.id}`} class="cm-anchor-nav-item">
          <span class="cm-anchor-nav-num">{section.num}</span>
          <span>{section.navLabel}</span>
        </a>
      ))}
    </nav>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="docs-hero">
      <div class="cm-tag">{content.hero.kicker}</div>
      <h1>{content.hero.title}<br /><span class="accent">{content.hero.titleAccent}</span> {content.hero.titleEnd}</h1>
      <p class="docs-body">{content.hero.body}</p>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ Companion Intro (before §01) ═══ -->
    <section class="docs-companion-intro">
      <div class="docs-inner">
        <div class="cm-tag">{content.companionIntro.kicker}</div>
        <h2>{content.companionIntro.title}</h2>
        <p class="docs-p" set:html={content.companionIntro.body1} />
        <p class="docs-p" set:html={content.companionIntro.body2} />

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>{content.companionIntro.startTitle}</span></h3>
        <ul class="docs-list">
          {content.companionIntro.startItems.map((item) => (
            <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span set:html={item} /></li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>{content.companionIntro.modesTitle}</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-table">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col">
            <div>Mode</div><div>Description</div>
          </div>
          {content.companionIntro.modes.map((m, i) => (
            <div class:list={["docs-table-row", "docs-table-2col", { "docs-table-row-first": i === 0 }]}>
              <div class="docs-table-label">{m.label}</div>
              <div class="docs-table-desc">{m.desc}</div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-rule">
          <div class="docs-callout-label">Rule of thumb · {content.companionIntro.ruleTitle}</div>
          <div class="docs-callout-body" set:html={content.companionIntro.ruleBody} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ §01 · Understanding the Window ═══ -->
    <section id="window" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-inner">
        <div class="cm-section-header-meta">
          <span class="cm-section-header-num">§ 01</span>
          <span class="cm-section-header-line"></span>
          <span>chapter</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Understanding the Window</h2>
        <p class="docs-lead">When cipher-mux starts, you see two areas: the grid in the centre, the status bar at the bottom. That's it for now.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>The Grid (Main Area)</span></h3>
        <p class="docs-p">The large central area. This is where your sessions live — each in its own cell. Think of a desk with multiple monitors: each monitor shows a separate Claude conversation.</p>
        <p class="docs-p">An empty cell shows a <span class="docs-mono">+</span> in the centre. Clicking it opens the <strong>Launcher Popup</strong> — your entry point for everything.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Launcher Popup · Three Tabs</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-table">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col"><div>Tab</div><div>Purpose</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-label">Presets</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Start specialised roles directly — all available presets as cards (Companion, Refinement, Cyber Factory, ...). Running single-instance presets are marked with a dot. Resume button for existing sessions.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Path</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Start a session with a custom project path. Folder picker, recently used paths, plus options: Shell Only · Skip Permissions · Resume · Fork.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Notes</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Open an existing note in this cell or create a new note.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-tip">
          <div class="docs-callout-label">Tip</div>
          <div class="docs-callout-body">Keyboard: <span class="docs-mono">Cmd+N</span> opens the Launcher popup in the next empty cell.</div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>The Status Bar (Bottom Edge)</span></h3>
        <p class="docs-p">Your command centre. From left to right:</p>
        <div class="docs-table">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col"><div>Element</div><div>What it does</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-label">Voice Pill</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Voice control on/off. LED shows status: off / green (ready) / red (recording) / yellow (processing).</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">columns +/-</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Add or remove grid columns. Maximum 7.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">rows +/-</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Add or remove grid rows. Maximum 3.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">workspaces</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Open workspace and persona editor.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">cyber factory</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Start/stop Cyber Factory. Dot indicator when active.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">bugreport</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Open bug report dialog.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">sidebar</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Show/hide sidebar. LED glows when content is waiting.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Theme Name</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Click cycles to the next visual theme.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">info</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Settings, shortcuts, feature list.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Version</div><div class="docs-table-desc">App version (right side, not clickable).</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ §02 · Sessions ═══ -->
    <section id="sessions" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-inner">
        <div class="cm-section-header-meta">
          <span class="cm-section-header-num">§ 02</span>
          <span class="cm-section-header-line"></span>
          <span>chapter</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Sessions — Your AI Workstations</h2>
        <p class="docs-lead">A session is a separate phone call with Claude. Its own memory (context window), its own files, its own task. Sessions are independent of each other.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Opening a Session — Three Ways</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-table">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col"><div>Way</div><div>How</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-label">Via Preset</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Click + → Tab "Presets" → Choose preset. Session starts with predefined behaviour, persona, and project context.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Via Path</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Click + → Tab "Path" → Choose or type folder → Start. Bare Claude session in the chosen directory.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Via Workspace</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Apply workspace — the grid is populated automatically. One click, everything is set up.</div></div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Cell Controls</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-table">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-3col"><div>Button</div><div>Action</div><div>Description</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-3col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-key">&uarr;</div><div class="docs-table-label-mid">Expand</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Expand cell to full grid height (only with 2+ rows).</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-3col"><div class="docs-table-key">&darr;</div><div class="docs-table-label-mid">Collapse</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Back to normal height.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-3col"><div class="docs-table-key">&hArr;</div><div class="docs-table-label-mid">Switch</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Switch project without closing the session.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-3col"><div class="docs-table-key">$</div><div class="docs-table-label-mid">Shell</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Open shell in project directory. No Claude, plain terminal.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-3col"><div class="docs-table-key">&times;</div><div class="docs-table-label-mid">Close</div><div class="docs-table-desc">End session and release cell.</div></div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Focus, Context, Crash Safety</span></h3>
        <ul class="docs-list">
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>Focus:</strong> Click the header bar to set focus. Keyboard input goes to the focused cell. Drag and drop swaps positions.</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>Context indicator:</strong> Green = plenty of room. Orange at 80% = getting tight. Red at 90% = nearly full, session will need to forget soon.</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>Crash safety:</strong> Sessions survive crashes thanks to tmux. On restart, a recovery dialog appears — resume or terminate.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ §03 · Grid ═══ -->
    <section id="grid" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-inner">
        <div class="cm-section-header-meta">
          <span class="cm-section-header-num">§ 03</span>
          <span class="cm-section-header-line"></span>
          <span>chapter</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Customising the Grid</h2>
        <p class="docs-lead">One to 21 cells. As many or as few as you need.</p>

        <ul class="docs-list">
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><span class="docs-mono">columns +/-</span> and <span class="docs-mono">rows +/-</span> in the status bar</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span>Minimum 1&times;1 (one cell), maximum 7&times;3 (21 cells)</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span>The window adjusts its size automatically</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span>With 2+ rows: <span class="docs-mono">&uarr;</span> stretches a cell to full height — useful for reading long outputs</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Typical Layouts</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-table">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col"><div>Layout</div><div>Use case</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-label">2&times;1</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Two sessions side by side — everyday standard.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">3&times;1</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Three columns — e.g. Frontend / Backend / Tests.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">2&times;2</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Four cells — Cyber Factory + three workers.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ §04 · Voice ═══ -->
    <section id="voice" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-inner">
        <div class="cm-section-header-meta">
          <span class="cm-section-header-num">§ 04</span>
          <span class="cm-section-header-line"></span>
          <span>chapter</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Voice Control</h2>
        <p class="docs-lead">Local speech recognition — no network, no cloud. Voice pill in the status bar or Ctrl+Shift+Space.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>LED Status</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-led-row">
          <div class="docs-led-item"><span class="docs-led-dot docs-led-off"></span><span class="docs-led-label">off</span><span class="docs-led-desc">Voice is disabled</span></div>
          <div class="docs-led-item"><span class="docs-led-dot docs-led-green"></span><span class="docs-led-label">green</span><span class="docs-led-desc">ready, not listening</span></div>
          <div class="docs-led-item"><span class="docs-led-dot docs-led-red"></span><span class="docs-led-label">red</span><span class="docs-led-desc">currently recording</span></div>
          <div class="docs-led-item"><span class="docs-led-dot docs-led-yellow"></span><span class="docs-led-label">yellow</span><span class="docs-led-desc">processing — please wait</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-rule">
          <div class="docs-callout-label">Rule of thumb · Important</div>
          <div class="docs-callout-body">Spoken text is inserted but <em>not sent automatically</em>. You can read, correct, then send via <span class="docs-mono">"submit"</span> or Enter.</div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Voice Commands · Text</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-table docs-table-compact">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col"><div>Say</div><div>Effect</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-label">"abschicken" / "absenden" / "senden"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Press Enter (send text).</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">"neue zeile"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Insert line break.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">anything else</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Transcribed and inserted as text.</div></div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Voice Commands · Scrolling</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-table docs-table-compact">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col"><div>Say</div><div>Effect</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-label">"hoch" / "rauf"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Scroll one page up.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">"runter" / "weiter"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Scroll one page down.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">"ganz hoch" / "anfang"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Scroll to top.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">"ganz runter" / "ende"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Scroll to bottom.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">"zum marker" / "lesestart"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Jump to the start of the last response.</div></div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Voice Commands · Grid Navigation</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-table docs-table-compact">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col"><div>Say</div><div>Effect</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-label">"grid hoch"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Focus cell above.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">"grid runter"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Focus cell below.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">"grid links"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Focus cell to the left.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">"grid rechts"</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Focus cell to the right.</div></div>
        </div>
        <p class="docs-p">Variants like <span class="docs-mono">grit</span>, <span class="docs-mono">zelle</span>, <span class="docs-mono">focus</span> are also recognised.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Voice Pin · Bluetooth Remote</span></h3>
        <ul class="docs-list">
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>Voice Pin:</strong> Pin voice input to a specific session — your voice always goes there, regardless of which cell is focused.</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>Bluetooth Clicker</strong> (e.g. AB Shutter). Auto mode: press = send immediately. Manual mode: press = start/stop recording, send explicitly.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ §05 · Sidebar ═══ -->
    <section id="sidebar" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-inner">
        <div class="cm-section-header-meta">
          <span class="cm-section-header-num">§ 05</span>
          <span class="cm-section-header-line"></span>
          <span>chapter</span>
        </div>
        <h2>The Sidebar</h2>
        <p class="docs-lead">Click 'sidebar' in the status bar. Multiple tabs, different functions.</p>

        <div class="docs-table">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col"><div>Tab</div><div>Content</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-label">Messages</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Messages between sessions — visible during multi-session work (Cyber Factory etc.).</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Background</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Sessions running but not visible in the grid. Cards with live preview (5s refresh). Click brings the session into the grid.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Notes</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Note browser. Search field, tag chips for filtering, double-click opens a note in the grid as an editor cell.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Companion Memory</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Stored memories from the Companion session. Searchable and viewable.</div></div>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-tip">
          <div class="docs-callout-label">Tip</div>
          <div class="docs-callout-body">The <span class="docs-mono">&#x29C9;</span> button at the top detaches the sidebar as its own window — ideal for multi-monitor setups.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ §06 · Notes ═══ -->
    <section id="notes" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-inner">
        <div class="cm-section-header-meta">
          <span class="cm-section-header-num">§ 06</span>
          <span class="cm-section-header-line"></span>
          <span>chapter</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Notes</h2>
        <p class="docs-lead">Markdown editor (CodeMirror) in grid cells. Headings, bold, italic, links, code blocks, block quotes.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Create, Save, Auto-Tags</span></h3>
        <ul class="docs-list">
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>New note:</strong> Via Launcher popup → Tab "Notes" → "New Note", or <span class="docs-mono">+</span> in the tab bar of an open editor</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>Save + Auto-Tagging:</strong> <span class="docs-mono">Cmd+S</span> — saves and automatically suggests tags (local AI model, max 5 tags per note)</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>Auto-Save:</strong> After 2 seconds of inactivity (without tagging)</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>Delete:</strong> Trash icon in the tab bar, with confirmation</span></li>
          <li><span class="docs-list-marker">&rsaquo;</span><span><strong>Handoff Notes:</strong> Special notes for knowledge transfer between sessions — when a session finishes its work, it hands over context to the next</span></li>
        </ul>

        <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-rule">
          <div class="docs-callout-label">Rule of thumb · Memory vs. Notes</div>
          <div class="docs-callout-body">What the user should see, share, or read in Obsidian is a <strong>Note</strong> (Markdown file). What belongs to internal run management (worker status, risk reviews, etc.) is <strong>Memory</strong> (not visible).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ §07 · Projects ═══ -->
    <section id="projects" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-inner">
        <div class="cm-section-header-meta">
          <span class="cm-section-header-num">§ 07</span>
          <span class="cm-section-header-line"></span>
          <span>chapter</span>
        </div>
        <h2>Projects and Project Structure</h2>
        <p class="docs-lead">Central directory as single source of truth for all projects. Standardised folder structure, three adoption modes for existing projects.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>CIPHER-MUX Hub · Default Structure</span></h3>
        <pre class="docs-terminal">project-name/
  .claude/              <span class="dim">Claude Code config</span>
  .cyber-factory/       <span class="dim">Run configuration</span>
  docs/specs/           <span class="dim">Detail specs with REQ IDs</span>
  docs/decisions/       <span class="dim">ADRs (architecture decisions)</span>
  docs/research/        <span class="dim">Research from Ideation Partner</span>
  docs/audit/           <span class="dim">Audit reports</span>
  src/                  <span class="dim">Source code</span>
  tests/                <span class="dim">Tests</span>
  .project-meta.json    <span class="dim">Phase, workspace, tags, purpose</span></pre>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Adopting Existing Projects · Three Modes</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-table">
          <div class="docs-table-header docs-table-2col"><div>Mode</div><div>What happens</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col docs-table-row-first"><div class="docs-table-label">Full Adoption</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Complete pack conventions are applied — all folders, ADRs, specs, .project-meta.json.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Pack-Light</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Adopt only individual components — e.g. just docs/specs or just .claude/.</div></div>
          <div class="docs-table-row docs-table-2col"><div class="docs-table-label">Inventory</div><div class="docs-table-desc">Audit only — pack doesn't touch anything, just documents what's there.</div></div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Starting a New Project</span></h3>
        <div class="docs-pipeline">
          <div class="docs-pipeline-step">Ideation Partner</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-step">Refinement</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-step">Cyber Factory</div>
        </div>
        <p class="docs-p">Lifecycle entry point: Ideation Partner collects the idea, Refinement sharpens the requirements, the Cyber Factory takes over scaffolding as part of the architect phase.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ §08 · Lifecycle ═══ -->
    <section id="lifecycle" class="docs-section">
      <div class="docs-inner">
        <div class="cm-section-header-meta">
          <span class="cm-section-header-num">§ 08</span>
          <span class="cm-section-header-line"></span>
          <span>chapter</span>
        </div>
        <h2>The Software Lifecycle — Presets</h2>
        <p class="docs-lead">Six specialised presets along the lifecycle. Each preset covers a phase and hands off cleanly to the next.</p>

        <div class="docs-pipeline">
          <div class="docs-pipeline-step">Ideation Partner</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-step">Refinement</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-step">Cyber Factory</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-step">Testing</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-step">Debugger</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="docs-pipeline-step">Audit</div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Ideation Partner</span></h3>
        <p class="docs-p">Takes raw ideas, researches (autonomously, with sub-agents), synthesises, and produces a structured requirements package.</p>
        <p class="docs-p"><strong>Phases:</strong> Seed → Research → Focus → Robustness Gate (Pre-Mortem) → Requirements Package.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Refinement</span></h3>
        <p class="docs-p">Systematically checks requirements for gaps, writes detail specs with REQ IDs and acceptance criteria.</p>
        <p class="docs-p"><strong>Phases:</strong> Required-field check → Gap audit → Validation → Sharpen requirements → Detail spec with REQ IDs → Handoff to Cyber Factory.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Cyber Factory</span></h3>
        <p class="docs-p">Architect and multi-session orchestrator in one. Receives the detail spec and coordinates the build with independent worker sessions.</p>
        <p class="docs-p"><strong>Phases:</strong> Read spec → Architect phase (subsystem decomposition, ADRs, scaffolding) → Wave plan → Start worker sessions (max 5 parallel, own git worktrees) → Monitoring (5-7 min cycles) → Escalation (5 levels) → Risk review → Wave cutover.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Testing Assistant</span></h3>
        <p class="docs-p">Systematically and adversarially tests implementation-ready waves. Fixes nothing — documents findings.</p>
        <p class="docs-p"><strong>Phases:</strong> Test run → Test quality audit → Adversarial probing → Security audit (OWASP Top 10) → Findings report. Handoff: with findings to Debugger, with "all green" to Audit.</p>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Debugger</span></h3>
        <p class="docs-p">Bugfixing specialist. Receives findings from the Testing Assistant or direct bug reports.</p>
        <p class="docs-p"><strong>Phases:</strong> Read findings → Clarify → Fix plan → Worker session for fix → Risk review → Verification (test must have been red, green after fix).</p>
        <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-warn">
          <div class="docs-callout-label">Warning</div>
          <div class="docs-callout-body">Maximum <strong>2 retries</strong> per fix. Then user escalation.</div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="docs-subhead"><span class="docs-subhead-dot"></span><span>Audit</span></h3>
        <p class="docs-p">Assesses whether a wave has reached release level. Fixes nothing, implements nothing.</p>
        <p class="docs-p"><strong>Phases:</strong> Read wave diff → Code review → Security audit → ADR consistency → Cognitive debt assessment → Release recommendation: <span class="docs-mono">Release</span> · <span class="docs-mono">Release after Fix</span> · <span class="docs-mono">Blocked</span>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

